adbhuta (in Mvy Kyoto ed. always adbhūta, 〔1277, 5043, 7164〕; but Mironov adbhuta without v.l.),
(1) adj. amazed, wonder-struck (in Skt. only astonishing, and so usually Pali abbhuta, but see Ap 〔109.24〕, CPD s.v.) āścaryabhūtā sma tathādbhutāś ca SP 〔110.12〕, we are amazed and astonished;
(2) nt., also adbhuta-dharma, m. (Pali abbhuta, ˚ta-dhamma), one of the divisions or types of literature in the Buddhist canon, marvel(s), itivṛttakaṃ jātakam adbhutaṃ ca SP 〔45.7〕; adbhutadharmaḥ Mvy 〔1277〕; ˚dharma, Dharmas 〔62〕, one of the nine pravacana. (Not in this sense, adbhutānāṃ ca dharmāṇāṃ viśuddhir upalabhyate Mv 〔i.175.17〕, of marvelous conditions or states.)
